WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 3.9 · Structure, Governance & Accountability
Coordination and internal communication

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Reliable hand-offs need a named recipient, an agreed output and a date.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Use meetings for decisions; share updates beforehand.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Agree what goes in chat, email and shared folders.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Keep one decision log everyone can read.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Vanita Weavers Cooperative (Cooperative · member-owned, India)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Vanita: every Friday the quality officer sends accepted pieces to the accounts clerk, so weavers are paid within 15 days.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You create your operating rhythm, channel rules and one critical hand-off.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
